list.append() + ''.join() improves report assembly from O(n²) to O(n)). 
• Space Complexity (50,000 lines): Reading the whole file via f.read() requires O(file size) memory—holding the raw 
string buffer plus a 50,000-element list of line strings simultaneously (~5–15 MB depending on line length). 
Streaming line-by-line via 'for line in f:' uses O(one line) auxiliary read buffer (~8 KB internal chunk buffer), which 
remains constant regardless of whether the file has 50,000 or 50,000,000 lines. 
