Task 3.2: Design a Custom Exception (2 Marks) 
• Definition: class InvalidRecord(Exception): pass — inherits from Exception (not BaseException) so standard 
application error handlers catch it while system exits/interrupts pass through. 
• Where Raised: Inside the low-level record parser function parse_line(line) whenever structural or domain 
validation fails (wrong column count, blank register number, or status outside {'P', 'A'}). 
• Where Handled: Inside the file-reading loop of summarise(path), which owns the file name and current 
line_no context needed to log (line_no, str(err)) and continue processing subsequent lines. 
Task 3.3: Use the Complete try Statement (3 Marks) 
