Task 4.1: Locate the Defects (2 Marks) 
• 1. Why earlier days are lost: save_returns() opens 'returns.log' with mode 'w' (write/truncate). Every daily call 
erases the existing file contents from previous days and writes only that day's books. 
• 2. Why books are joined together on one line: read().split('\n') strips all newline characters from each book 
title, and log.write(b) writes each string directly without appending '\n', concatenating all titles into a single 
continuous string (e.g., 'BookABookBBookC'). 
• 3. What happens to open files when write() fails or exceptions occur: Because neither open('returns.log', 'w') 
nor open(day_file) uses a with context manager, an exception during log.write(b) (such as Disk Full OSError or 
TypeError on non-string data) aborts save_returns() before log.close() is reached, leaving the file descriptor 
open and buffered data unflushed. Furthermore, process() catches only FileNotFoundError and lets write 
errors crash the program without logging the failure. 
